<title>UK: GUS in technical bounce after sell order.</title>
<headline>GUS in technical bounce after sell order.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in home shopping group Great Universal Stores Plc rebounded from recent weakness on Monday after a large sell order overhanging the market had been completed, dealers said.</p>
<p>The shares were up 12p to 602p by 1200 GMT.  </p>
<p>&quot;There's been a sell order hanging over the market for the last few days which is now gone,&quot; one dealer said. &quot;The shares are up on a technical bounce,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>Last week GUS shares fell 25p, or four percent, from 615p.</p>
<p>--Elaine Hardcastle, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
</text>
